Package: letsmash
Version: @VERSION@
Architecture: @ARCH@
Maintainer: @MAINTAINER@
Installed-Size: @INSTALLED_SIZE@
Depends: @DEPENDS@
Section: x11
Priority: optional
Homepage: https://letsma.sh
Description: Mash, a desktop workspace for AI coding agents
 Mash is an isolated desktop environment for AI coding agents: a pinned
 terminal frontend, a Herdr workspace with panes and tabs, the Pi agent,
 and the Fresh editor, all sharing one writable data folder in ~/.mash.
 .
 The macOS build ships as a signed disk image; this package is the Linux
 build for Ubuntu 24.04 with GNOME on Wayland or Xorg.
 .
 Product files live in /opt/letsmash and are read-only. Everything Mash
 writes lives under ~/.mash, which the package never touches: upgrades
 and removal leave your configuration, credentials and workspaces alone.
